Notebook[{Cell["ModularFormDefinition", "ObjectName"], 
  Cell["ModularFormDefinition[{f1, ...}, var, opts] parses a modular-form \
definition held, replacing var and the declared NormalizationParameters by \
inert atoms.\nModularFormDefinition[qexp] defines a form by the explicitly \
finite QExpansionData qexp.", "Usage"], Cell["Status: Alpha.", "Notes"], 
  Cell["ModularFormDefinition[{f1, ...}, var, opts] parses a modular-form \
definition held: the components (a literal list, or a symbol whose stored \
value is the list) may use var, numeric constants, declared \
NormalizationParameters and the scalar ingredients ScalarModularExpression \
and HypergeometricK.", "Notes"], Cell["ModularFormDefinition[qexp] defines a \
form by an explicitly finite QExpansionData (a literal value or a symbol \
bound to it); a jet defines only its known coefficients.", "Notes"], 
  Cell["Undeclared symbols fail with UndeclaredSymbol; executable or \
unsupported heads, symbols with DownValues and non-lists fail with \
InvalidDefinition. Options: Coordinate, NormalizationParameters, FamilyID.", 
   "Notes"], Cell["See Also", "SeeAlsoSection"], 
  Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["CreateModularForm", BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", 
